window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-030.json",{"day":30,"title":"Finding a Future in an Old Neighborhood","targetWords":[{"word":"dig","gloss":"挖","context":"Workers would dig beneath the pavement, pave damaged lanes, and insure contractors against accidents.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"excel","gloss":"表现出色","context":"Retired engineers could excel as mentors, while younger workers learned to complement technical knowledge with patient conversation.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"leak","gloss":"漏水","context":"A water leak could stain a ceiling, and overflowing bins made it difficult to dispose of household waste safely.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"alleviate","gloss":"减轻","context":"Planners needed to alleviate these anxieties before asking everyone to comply with new rules.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"comply","gloss":"遵守","context":"Planners needed to alleviate these anxieties before asking everyone to comply with new rules.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"commute","gloss":"通勤","context":"Residents needed somewhere to dwell safely and a reasonable way to commute, not a contest over whose frustration was more legitimate.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"compute","gloss":"计算","context":"A local college offered to enroll residents in practical courses and help them compute energy savings after repairs.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"dwell","gloss":"居住","context":"Residents needed somewhere to dwell safely and a reasonable way to commute, not a contest over whose frustration was more legitimate.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"shout","gloss":"喊叫","context":"A promoter tried to hijack a community event, and a dispute over parking produced a shout, then a scream.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"cling","gloss":"紧贴","context":"People can cling to an ineffective method when correction feels like humiliation.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"drown","gloss":"淹没","context":"Planners learned that renewal must not drown local voices in technical confidence.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"spark","gloss":"激起","context":"A spill from old pipes could spark anger as well as health concerns.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"scream","gloss":"喊叫","context":"A promoter tried to hijack a community event, and a dispute over parking produced a shout, then a scream.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"revenge","gloss":"报复","context":"Nor would they seek revenge on a shopkeeper who publicly called the plan a curse.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"coincide","gloss":"同时发生","context":"The final reopening was scheduled to coincide with a neighborhood festival.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"depart","gloss":"离开","context":"As old lamps began to glow, families chose to depart slowly rather than hurry away.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"insult","gloss":"侮辱","context":"It also addressed interpersonal habits: instructors should not insult beginners, scold them for asking questions, or let a careless joke hook them into embarrassment.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"lodge","gloss":"暂住","context":"One family might have to emigrate to find affordable housing elsewhere; another had nowhere to lodge during construction.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"subscribe","gloss":"订阅","context":"Volunteers would dedicate a restored courtyard to former residents, while visitors could subscribe to a public maintenance bulletin.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"stain","gloss":"染污","context":"A water leak could stain a ceiling, and overflowing bins made it difficult to dispose of household waste safely.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"complement","gloss":"补充","context":"Retired engineers could excel as mentors, while younger workers learned to complement technical knowledge with patient conversation.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"confess","gloss":"承认","context":"The project would succeed only if learners felt able to confess uncertainty before making a dangerous mistake.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"disclose","gloss":"揭露","context":"It should disclose the choices honestly, including the costs that an attractive drawing of the future conveniently left unseen.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"doom","gloss":"使遭殃","context":"Residents asked whether inspections would omit inaccessible rooms, since a flaw hidden there could eventually doom the entire building.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"enroll","gloss":"使入学","context":"A local college offered to enroll residents in practical courses and help them compute energy savings after repairs.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"hook","gloss":"使陷入","context":"It also addressed interpersonal habits: instructors should not insult beginners, scold them for asking questions, or let a careless joke hook them into embarrassment.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"inhabit","gloss":"居住","context":"Yet some feared the project would displace the people who inhabit the area and have kept it alive.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"renovate","gloss":"翻新","context":"When a city decided to renovate an old neighborhood, residents were promised better homes and a brisk recovery in local business.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"dispose","gloss":"处理掉","context":"A water leak could stain a ceiling, and overflowing bins made it difficult to dispose of household waste safely.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"hijack","gloss":"劫持","context":"A promoter tried to hijack a community event, and a dispute over parking produced a shout, then a scream.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"await","gloss":"等候","context":"People may await better housing with hope and still question its price.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"insure","gloss":"投保","context":"Workers would dig beneath the pavement, pave damaged lanes, and insure contractors against accidents.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"pave","gloss":"铺路","context":"Workers would dig beneath the pavement, pave damaged lanes, and insure contractors against accidents.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"spill","gloss":"泄漏","context":"A spill from old pipes could spark anger as well as health concerns.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"uncover","gloss":"揭开","context":"Teams had to uncover buried utility lines before beginning repairs.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"displace","gloss":"迫使搬迁","context":"Yet some feared the project would displace the people who inhabit the area and have kept it alive.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"echo","gloss":"回荡","context":"Rumors of deliberate favoritism began to echo through social media.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"erupt","gloss":"爆发","context":"During construction, trouble began to erupt around the market.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"forge","gloss":"锻造","context":"Training included how to forge a safe metal fitting and prevent an electrical fault.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"glow","gloss":"发光","context":"As old lamps began to glow, families chose to depart slowly rather than hurry away.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"heal","gloss":"愈合","context":"The place had started to heal, though nobody claimed all conflict had disappeared.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"refute","gloss":"反驳","context":"Officials chose to refute false claims while acknowledging real delays.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"scold","gloss":"斥责","context":"It also addressed interpersonal habits: instructors should not insult beginners, scold them for asking questions, or let a careless joke hook them into embarrassment.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"brisk","gloss":"迅速的","context":"When a city decided to renovate an old neighborhood, residents were promised better homes and a brisk recovery in local business.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"curse","gloss":"灾祸","context":"Nor would they seek revenge on a shopkeeper who publicly called the plan a curse.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"evade","gloss":"逃避","context":"They would not expel critics from meetings or evade awkward questions about who benefited.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"omit","gloss":"省略","context":"Residents asked whether inspections would omit inaccessible rooms, since a flaw hidden there could eventually doom the entire building.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"dedicate","gloss":"献给","context":"Volunteers would dedicate a restored courtyard to former residents, while visitors could subscribe to a public maintenance bulletin.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"emigrate","gloss":"移民","context":"One family might have to emigrate to find affordable housing elsewhere; another had nowhere to lodge during construction.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"expel","gloss":"驱逐","context":"They would not expel critics from meetings or evade awkward questions about who benefited.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"When a city decided to renovate an old neighborhood, residents were promised better homes and a brisk recovery in local business. Yet some feared the project would displace the people who inhabit the area and have kept it alive. One family might have to emigrate to find affordable housing elsewhere; another had nowhere to lodge during construction. Planners needed to alleviate these anxieties before asking everyone to comply with new rules. A meeting should not end with officials telling worried residents to stop complaining. It should disclose the choices honestly, including the costs that an attractive drawing of the future conveniently left unseen.","zh":"城市决定翻新旧社区时，居民得到改善住房、迅速复兴商铺的承诺。但有人担心，项目会驱逐那些住在这里、维持社区活力的人。一家可能得移居国外才能找到可负担住处，另一家施工期间无处暂住。规划者在要求大家遵守新规定前，需要缓解焦虑。会议不应以官员要求居民停止抱怨结束，而应诚实公开选择，包括漂亮未来图景方便地隐藏的成本。"},{"en":"The area had genuine problems. A water leak could stain a ceiling, and overflowing bins made it difficult to dispose of household waste safely. Workers would dig beneath the pavement, pave damaged lanes, and insure contractors against accidents. A spill from old pipes could spark anger as well as health concerns. Teams had to uncover buried utility lines before beginning repairs. Residents asked whether inspections would omit inaccessible rooms, since a flaw hidden there could eventually doom the entire building. The answer required evidence, not a reassuring slogan that nobody would be able to check afterward.","zh":"这里确实有问题。漏水可能染污天花板，垃圾桶满溢让安全处理生活废物困难。工人要开挖路面、铺修损坏小巷，承包商也要投保意外险。旧管道泄漏既会带来健康风险，也会激起愤怒。团队维修前必须查明埋藏的管线。居民询问，检查会不会漏掉无法进入的房间，因为其中隐藏的缺陷最终可能使整个建筑受损。答案需要证据，而非事后无人能核查的安抚口号。"},{"en":"A local college offered to enroll residents in practical courses and help them compute energy savings after repairs. Retired engineers could excel as mentors, while younger workers learned to complement technical knowledge with patient conversation. Training included how to forge a safe metal fitting and prevent an electrical fault. It also addressed interpersonal habits: instructors should not insult beginners, scold them for asking questions, or let a careless joke hook them into embarrassment. People can cling to an ineffective method when correction feels like humiliation. The project would succeed only if learners felt able to confess uncertainty before making a dangerous mistake.","zh":"当地学院让居民参加实用课程，帮助计算修缮后的节能效果。退休工程师成为出色导师，年轻工人学习用耐心交流补充技术知识。培训包括安全锻造金属接头、防止电气故障，也涉及人际习惯：教师不能侮辱初学者、因提问责备他们，或让轻率笑话把他们推入尴尬。当纠正像羞辱，人就可能固守无效方法。只有学习者敢在造成危险错误前承认不确定，项目才会成功。"},{"en":"During construction, trouble began to erupt around the market. A promoter tried to hijack a community event, and a dispute over parking produced a shout, then a scream. Rumors of deliberate favoritism began to echo through social media. Officials chose to refute false claims while acknowledging real delays. They would not expel critics from meetings or evade awkward questions about who benefited. Nor would they seek revenge on a shopkeeper who publicly called the plan a curse. Residents needed somewhere to dwell safely and a reasonable way to commute, not a contest over whose frustration was more legitimate.","zh":"施工期间，市场周边矛盾爆发。推广商试图劫持社区活动的主导权，停车争议从喊叫变成尖叫。关于故意偏袒的传言在社交媒体回荡。官员反驳错误说法，同时承认实际延误。他们不把批评者赶出会议，也不回避谁受益的问题，更不报复公开称计划为灾祸的店主。居民需要安全居所和合理通勤，而不是比拼谁的挫折更有正当性。"},{"en":"The final reopening was scheduled to coincide with a neighborhood festival. Volunteers would dedicate a restored courtyard to former residents, while visitors could subscribe to a public maintenance bulletin. As old lamps began to glow, families chose to depart slowly rather than hurry away. The place had started to heal, though nobody claimed all conflict had disappeared. Planners learned that renewal must not drown local voices in technical confidence. People may await better housing with hope and still question its price. Listening to both emotions is essential when a city wants to improve a neighborhood without destroying the relationships that give it meaning.","zh":"重新开放安排在社区节庆当天。志愿者把修复庭院献给昔日居民，游客可以订阅公开维修简报。旧灯亮起，家庭缓缓离开，并不急着走。这里开始愈合，但没人声称冲突全已消失。规划者明白，更新不能用技术自信淹没本地声音。人们可以满怀希望等候好住房，同时质疑代价。城市若想改善社区又不毁掉赋予其意义的关系，倾听这两种情绪都至关重要。"}],"previous":29,"next":31});
